  "instructions": "## Forward pass by hand\n\nEverything a network does forward is a weighted sum, a bias and a non-linearity. Implement the pieces in plain Python.\n\n1. `relu(x)` and `sigmoid(x)` on single numbers.\n2. `dense(x, W, b)`: for input vector `x`, weight matrix `W` (one row per output unit) and bias vector `b`, return the vector of `Σ_j W[i][j]·x[j] + b[i]`.\n3. `softmax(z)`: subtract the maximum before exponentiating (numerical stability) and return probabilities that sum to 1.\n4. `forward(x, W1, b1, W2, b2)`: dense → relu on every element → dense → softmax.",
